<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<ul>
<li>&quot;Warbalang&quot; is a nonsense word that came to my head, possibly an artifact of the knowledge of the &quot;Berbalang&quot;, a Filipino mythical beast. In-universe, I imagine it was coined by one of the children, so if it turns into something distracting in your own language, consider this a baseline for a new word.</li>
<li>Pastor Warbler's dialogue was intended as an emulation of the archetypal southern US hellfire and salvation preacher you'd see at outdoor revivals, while the Unknown Man/Elder Rockwell is the archetypal &quot;behind the pew&quot; preacher. Feel free to explore your own language's quirks wrt such things.</li>
<li>Researcher Ford is referred to with gender neutral pronouns in the non-dialogue logs. I intended this because I saw her as a trans woman who hadn't realized she's trans/come out and just wanted to avoid dysphoria. Make of it however your language does that kind of thing.</li>
<li>This skip is meant to explore the American Religious Right, the &quot;Troubled Teen&quot; industry, and the contradictory use of brutality in pursuit of propriety. Absolutely feel free to add or cut stuff to get the point across to non-American audiences.</li>
</ul>
