														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4800740">
									

<p>My favorite SCPs are those that get under my skin but never offer any final resolution. They itch. I'll spend days after reading worrying over them, trying to puzzle out a solution. Sometimes I'll have some insight, but the best ones leave me perplexed. Sometimes, years later, an image from these will pop into my head in a quiet moment - as I'm waking up, as I'm spacing out at my desk - and I'll wonder what, exactly, was up with that really weird SCP. You know. The one with the kid heads. The one with dead girl and the politician appearing in dreams. The ones that almost but don't quite form a coherent image. That feel like they <em>should</em>. There are alarming details but no obvious connections between them.</p>
<p>How does it all fit together? What am I missing? Would knowing ease the unease or chill it into full-on dread?</p>
<p>This has that feeling. As you continue this, please withhold explanations and connections. Resist the temptation to show off elaborate dioramas. It will be much better that way.</p>

